@* AppToggleGroup.razor — shared reusable two-(or-more)-option segmented
   control (CLAUDE.md §3.1), used by Screen B's "توزيع الأسئلة" mode switch
   (اختيار متعدد / سحب وإملاء) and any future mutually-exclusive choice.

   ============================================================================
   BUILT CUSTOM, NOT WRAPPING MudToggleGroup<T> — VERIFIED, NOT GUESSED
   ============================================================================
   MudBlazor 8.7.0 does ship MudToggleGroup<T>/MudToggleItem<T> (confirmed in
   the installed MudBlazor.xml), and its SelectionMode.SingleSelection visual
   look is exactly right (filled-primary for the selected item, outlined-
   primary for the rest) — so it was tried first, per CLAUDE.md rule 1.
   Rendered a live instance and read its actual DOM (dotnet watch hot-reload
   can patch an EXISTING page's render tree — confirmed by editing
   QuestionDistribution.razor directly and inspecting via a headless
   browser — but does NOT pick up a brand-new @page route without a full
   rebuild neither watch nor a manual `dotnet build` could complete while the
   dev server held the output lock; noted here in case a future pass hits
   the same wall). The real output:
     <div role="group" class="mud-toggle-group ...">
       <button role="checkbox" aria-checked="true"  class="...mud-button-filled-primary...">اختيار متعدد</button>
       <button role="checkbox" aria-checked="false" class="...mud-button-outlined-primary...">سحب وإملاء</button>
     </div>
   MudToggleGroup hardcodes role="group" on the wrapper and role="checkbox"
   on every item, in EVERY SelectionMode (including SingleSelection) —
   neither role nor aria-checked's semantics are exposed as an overridable
   parameter anywhere in the documented API. For a mutually-exclusive
   two-option choice this is the WRONG ARIA (a screen reader announces two
   independent checkboxes, not one exclusive choice), which is exactly what
   this instruction asked to avoid. Patching it via attribute splatting would
   mean fighting an undocumented internal (CLAUDE.md rule 3's spirit extended
   to ARIA, not just CSS specificity) for a two-button control that's cheap
   to own outright — so this is a small custom component, plain semantic
   <button> elements with the real ARIA radiogroup/radio pattern wired by
   hand, reusing MudToggleGroup's proven VISUAL result (filled-primary /
   outlined-primary) via the same underlying tokens instead of its markup.
   ============================================================================

   ACCESSIBILITY — WAI-ARIA radiogroup pattern (CLAUDE.md §6):
     - Wrapper: role="radiogroup" with a required AriaLabel (the visible
       "توزيع الأسئلة" section title is a separate heading, not this
       control's own accessible name, so it's passed explicitly).
     - Each item: role="radio" + aria-checked, native <button> (semantic
       HTML first) so Enter/Space activation and the disabled state come
       free from the platform.
     - Roving tabindex: only the SELECTED item is tabindex="0"; the rest are
       "-1", so Tab enters/exits the whole group in one stop — the real APG
       radiogroup pattern, not just "every button is its own tab stop".
     - Arrow keys move BOTH selection and focus together (APG radiogroup
       behavior, same as a native <input type="radio"> group) — see
       OnKeyDownAsync. Deliberately simplified to "any arrow key moves to
       the OTHER item" (index+1 mod Count): correct and unambiguous for
       exactly 2 options (this component's only real usage today), but NOT
       real directional/RTL-aware Left/Right logic — flag and extend this if
       AppToggleGroup is ever reused with 3+ options.
     - Touch target ≥44×44 CSS px and a visible focus ring on top of the
       item's own selected/unselected colors (the shared --focus-ring-*
       tokens, same standing rule as every other interactive component in
       this file) — never color alone, never a substitute for the ring.
   ============================================================================ *@
@typeparam T

<div class="app-toggle-group" role="radiogroup" aria-label="@AriaLabel">
    @for (var i = 0; i < Options.Count; i++)
    {
        var index = i;
        var option = Options[index];
        var isSelected = EqualityComparer<T>.Default.Equals(option.Value, SelectedValue);
        <button @ref="_itemRefs[index]"
                type="button"
                role="radio"
                aria-checked="@(isSelected ? "true" : "false")"
                tabindex="@(isSelected ? 0 : -1)"
                class="@GetItemClass(isSelected)"
                disabled="@Disabled"
                @onclick="@(() => SelectAsync(index))"
                @onkeydown="@(e => OnKeyDownAsync(e, index))">
            @if (option.IconPosition == Adornment.Start)
            {
                <MudIcon Icon="@option.Icon" Color="Color.Inherit" Class="app-toggle-group__icon" aria-hidden="true" />
            }
            <span class="app-toggle-group__label">@option.Label</span>
            @if (option.IconPosition == Adornment.End)
            {
                <MudIcon Icon="@option.Icon" Color="Color.Inherit" Class="app-toggle-group__icon" aria-hidden="true" />
            }
        </button>
    }
</div>

@code {
    [Parameter, EditorRequired] public IReadOnlyList<AppToggleOption<T>> Options { get; set; } = Array.Empty<AppToggleOption<T>>();

    [Parameter] public T SelectedValue { get; set; } = default!;
    [Parameter] public EventCallback<T> SelectedValueChanged { get; set; }

    [Parameter] public bool Disabled { get; set; }

    /// Required: role="radiogroup"'s own accessible name. The visible
    /// section title next to this control (e.g. "توزيع الأسئلة") is a
    /// separate heading element, not programmatically tied to this group,
    /// so it must be repeated here rather than assumed.
    [Parameter, EditorRequired] public string AriaLabel { get; set; } = string.Empty;

    private readonly List<ElementReference> _itemRefs = new();

    protected override void OnParametersSet()
    {
        while (_itemRefs.Count < Options.Count)
        {
            _itemRefs.Add(default);
        }
    }

    private string GetItemClass(bool isSelected) =>
        isSelected
            ? "app-toggle-group__item app-toggle-group__item--selected"
            : "app-toggle-group__item";

    private Task SelectAsync(int index)
    {
        if (Disabled)
        {
            return Task.CompletedTask;
        }
        return SelectedValueChanged.HasDelegate
            ? SelectedValueChanged.InvokeAsync(Options[index].Value)
            : Task.CompletedTask;
    }

    /// Any arrow key moves to "the other" item — see the header comment's
    /// ACCESSIBILITY note on why (index+1) % Count is correct only because
    /// this component has exactly 2 options today.
    private async Task OnKeyDownAsync(KeyboardEventArgs e, int index)
    {
        if (Disabled || Options.Count < 2)
        {
            return;
        }
        if (e.Key is "ArrowLeft" or "ArrowRight" or "ArrowUp" or "ArrowDown")
        {
            var nextIndex = (index + 1) % Options.Count;
            await SelectAsync(nextIndex);
            await _itemRefs[nextIndex].FocusAsync();
        }
    }
}
